Subject: Translator: Rename variables that are extracted from switch

When pruning dead code, declarations in switch statements (when in dead
code) are extracted and declared above the switch.  This is because
another case may use that variable.

In the MSL generator, every declaration in a switch is extracted.

In either case, the variable that was previously nested in switch may
shadow an existing variable and moving the declaration out is not always
correct.  This change replaces these variables with ones that have
generated names to avoid such name collisions.

This bug does not affect the IR since variables never shadow.

Bug: chromium:568896486
Bug: chromium:568896063
